From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Giuseppe Maggio <jertlok@proton.me>
Date: Mon, 10 Aug 2026 11:54:22 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: wcd934x: check the SLIMbus stream setup in trigger

wcd934x_trigger() discards the return of both slim_stream_prepare() and
slim_stream_enable(), so a stream that the bus refuses to set up still
reports a successful START. The PCM then runs to completion with correct
timing and delivers silence, and nothing anywhere says why.

That is the whole failure signature of a capture on this codec, and it is
the state the driver is left in whenever the SLIMbus side fails for any
reason -- an unsupported presence rate, a port that will not connect, a
controller that rejects the channel definition.

Check both, unprepare the stream if enabling it fails, and return the
error so the PCM layer fails the start where the fault actually is.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Giuseppe Maggio <jertlok@proton.me>
---
 sound/soc/codecs/wcd934x.c | 16 ++++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/sound/soc/codecs/wcd934x.c b/sound/soc/codecs/wcd934x.c
index 26c4f015df00..9687a074e305 100644
--- a/sound/soc/codecs/wcd934x.c
+++ b/sound/soc/codecs/wcd934x.c
@@ -1940,8 +1940,20 @@ static int wcd934x_trigger(struct snd_pcm_substream *substream, int cmd,
 				ret);
 			return ret;
 		}
-		slim_stream_prepare(dai_data->sruntime, cfg);
-		slim_stream_enable(dai_data->sruntime);
+		ret = slim_stream_prepare(dai_data->sruntime, cfg);
+		if (ret) {
+			dev_err(wcd->dev, "Error preparing SLIM stream: %d\n",
+				ret);
+			return ret;
+		}
+
+		ret = slim_stream_enable(dai_data->sruntime);
+		if (ret) {
+			dev_err(wcd->dev, "Error enabling SLIM stream: %d\n",
+				ret);
+			slim_stream_unprepare(dai_data->sruntime);
+			return ret;
+		}
 		break;
 	case SNDRV_PCM_TRIGGER_STOP:
 	case SNDRV_PCM_TRIGGER_SUSPEND:
